    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One Home Chord, Three Ways",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "modes-one-home-three-ways"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " left Ionian's vamp row empty — Ionian has no characteristic note, so there was no second chord that could assert one. Aeolian's row here isn't empty: "
        },
        {
          "text": "Am",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "–"
        },
        {
          "text": "F",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " is a real vamp. But it's the only one of the three that can't pin its own mode down, and that gap is worth tracing all the way through."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "text": "D",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " major — "
          },
          {
            "text": "D F# A",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " — sits inside Ionian, Mixolydian and Dorian. "
          },
          {
            "text": "Am",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": "–"
          },
          {
            "text": "D",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " rules out Aeolian and Phrygian, both of which need an "
          },
          {
            "text": "F",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " where "
          },
          {
            "text": "D",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " needs an "
          },
          {
            "text": "F#",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " — and what rules out Ionian and Mixolydian instead is the minor home chord, not this one chord's notes."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "text": "F",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " major — "
          },
          {
            "text": "F A C",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " — sits inside both Aeolian and Phrygian. "
          },
          {
            "text": "Am",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": "–"
          },
          {
            "text": "F",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " rules out Dorian and stops there — it doesn't separate Aeolian from Phrygian."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "text": "Bb",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " major — "
          },
          {
            "text": "Bb D F",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " — sits inside Phrygian, and just one other of the seven, whose home chord isn't "
          },
          {
            "text": "Am",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": ". "
          },
          {
            "text": "Am",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": "–"
          },
          {
            "text": "Bb",
            "marks": ["code"]
          },
          {
            "text": " does pin Phrygian down."
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That's exactly what having no characteristic note costs Aeolian."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What separates the three when you're actually playing is one note apiece — the windows underneath are the same five you've always had. Dorian, land on the "
        },
        {
          "text": "6",
          "marks": [
            "code",
            {
              "type": "color",
              "tone": "amber"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Phrygian, land on the "
        },
        {
          "text": "b2",
          "marks": [
            "code",
            {
              "type": "color",
              "tone": "rose"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Aeolian gives you nothing to lean on, which is the point of it — and the one note to move through rather than land on is the "
        },
        {
          "text": "b6",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
